---
// Structure/tokens ported from ~/Downloads/Colophon Page.dc.html. Real
// links throughout, not the mockup's placeholder "#" hrefs: the repo, the
// live AGENTS.md, and the worked example in "the supervision loop" section
// — the mockup already used "Stop hiding the seams" as its example essay
// before that essay existed; it published for real this session, so the
// link is no longer hypothetical. Stamp copy matches AuthorshipStamp.astro
// and docs/04-ai-first.md §3 exactly rather than the mockup's own wording.
// Last checklist item from docs/04 §8 — everything else there already shipped.
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const seamsPost = (await getCollection("posts")).find((p) => p.id === "field-notes/stop-hiding-the-seams");

const stamps = [
  { name: "human", detail: "Zack wrote it. A bot may have fetched a link or fixed a typo." },
  { name: "duet", detail: "AI drafted it under my direction; I reshaped and edited it. This is the default." },
  {
    name: "bot",
    detail: "An agent generated it end to end (changelogs, data-driven posts); I reviewed it before it published.",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="How this site is made — zackglaser.com"
  description="The operating manual for this site's AI collaboration: what the bots do, what's mine alone, and the receipts that make it checkable, not just claimed."
>
  <div class="colophon-page" style="--accent:var(--pillar-workshop)">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">colophon</div>
      <h1 class="h1">How this site is made.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Most of the words on this site were drafted by AI, riding along with me. I don't hide that. This page is the
        operating manual — what the bots actually do, what they're not allowed to touch, and what I catch when I
        check their work.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="col-label">what rides along</div>
        <p>
          Drafting, research, scaffolding, and most of the commits on this site come from AI assistants working
          under direction — Claude, mainly, in a few different modes: chatting through an idea with me, or working
          directly in the codebase with the repo open.
        </p>
        <p>
          What they're allowed to do: propose structure, write first drafts, build components, fix bugs, commit
          changes. What they're not allowed to do: decide what I believe, or ship anything I haven't read.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card col-card-mine">
        <div class="col-label">what's mine</div>
        <p>
          Judgment is not delegated. Every position this site takes, every call on what publishes and when, and
          anything that leans on my name has a human behind it — me.
        </p>
        <p>
          A bot can draft an argument; whether the argument is one I'll stand behind is not a bot's decision. If
          something here is wrong, that's on me, not on "the AI."
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">the supervision loop, with a real example</div>
    <div class="example-card">
      <p>
        Here's an actual one, not a hypothetical. The essay{" "}
        {seamsPost && (
          <a href={`/${seamsPost.id}`} class="inline-link">
            "Stop hiding the seams"
          </a>
        )}{" "}
        started as a one-line prompt: I wanted to write about why this site treats AI collaboration as something to
        celebrate rather than disguise. Claude drafted a structure and a full essay from that.
      </p>
      <p>
        I made two calls before a word was written — which section of the site it belonged in, and how long it
        should run — and the draft came back matching both. The editing after that wasn't about fixing the argument;
        it was about making the <em>delivery</em> honest, too: making sure the essay's claim about auditable process
        was actually true of the process that produced it, not just a claim the essay made about itself. That turned
        into this page.
      </p>
      <div class="loop-strip">
        <div class="loop-step">direction up front</div>
        <div class="loop-arrow">→</div>
        <div class="loop-step">a full draft</div>
        <div class="loop-arrow">→</div>
        <div class="loop-step loop-step-active">
          a human read that checks whether it's <em>right</em>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">what the stamps mean</div>
    <p class="stamps-intro">Every post on this site carries a small marker near the byline.</p>
    <div class="stamps-row">
      {
        stamps.map((s) => (
          <div class="stamp-card">
            <div class="stamp-badge">{s.name}</div>
            <p class="stamp-detail">{s.detail}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="note">None of the three change who's accountable for what got published. That's always me.</p>

    <div class="section-label">the receipts</div>
    <div class="receipts-card">
      <p>
        This isn't a claim you have to take on trust. The repo behind this site is public, and every commit a bot
        made carries a <code>Co-Authored-By</code> trailer, so you can see exactly which changes came from a bot and
        which didn't.
      </p>
      <p>
        The actual instructions the bots work under are public too —{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/thirdth/zackglaser-com/blob/main/AGENTS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">
          AGENTS.md
        </a>{" "}
        — which is rarer than it should be. Most sites that mention "AI-assisted" don't publish the instructions
        their AI is running under. This one does.
      </p>
      <div class="receipt-links-row">
        <a href="https://github.com/thirdth/zackglaser-com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="receipt-link">
          [ view the repo ]
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/thirdth/zackglaser-com/blob/main/AGENTS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="receipt-link">
          [ read AGENTS.md ]
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .colophon-page {
    max-width: 840px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 36px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .lead {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }

  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .col-card {
    background: var(--color-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }
  .col-card-mine {
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .col-label {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .col-card p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .col-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .example-card {
    background: var(--color-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .example-card p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .example-card p:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .inline-link {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ink-soft);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
  }
  .inline-link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .loop-strip {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .loop-step {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    padding: 6px 14px;
  }
  .loop-step-active {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .loop-arrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .stamps-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .stamps-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .stamp-card {
    background: var(--color-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .stamp-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    padding: 4px 12px;
    align-self: flex-start;
  }
  .stamp-detail {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  .receipts-card {
    background: var(--color-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .receipts-card p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .receipts-card p:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .receipts-card code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 2px 6px;
  }
  .receipt-links-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .receipt-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-input);
    padding: 8px 14px;
  }
  .receipt-link:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .stamps-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .h1 {
      font-size: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
